    "humanReview": "Unreviewed; difficulty is an author estimate.",
    "entrance": "Low western boarding ledge.",
    "exit": "Eastern gallery above the horizontal sunbeam.",
    "solution": "Catch the vertical carrier from the west and swing right through the low tally. Reel in as it climbs. Near its upper station, pay out and gently pump right so the knight hangs just outside its right side, about five tiles below its lower corner. Updash along that side and hold Jump as the burst finishes. The last residual rise reaches the moving wall during the new grace window, producing the rightward wallbounce. The carrier also shades the horizontal beam during departure; the twin overhead beams make standing on its top unsafe.",
    "nearestExisting": "F34 creates a fixed phase wall and trades it for a landing. F37 transfers between moving rings. Here the same carrier is transport, a moving beam shade, and the wall contacted after the dash has finished; rope length sets whether its lower corner arrives in time.",
    "novelty": "The attachment must be lengthened before it can be abandoned: maximum reeling is not the best launch. The knight returns upward along the carrier instead of simply flinging away from the rope.",
    "designNotes": "The intended tape genuinely emits late-wallbounce on post-dash contact, not only the legacy wallbounce. Buffered Jump spans the arrival, and several nearby payout/aim positions are saved. Conventional earlier wallbounces remain valid if a player arranges them. No named-tech exit condition.",
